35,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"My research reveals significant financial risks. Transport costs fluctuate drastically based on distance, and whole-building lets use non-refundable deposits based on headcounts. This means late cancellations would unfairly burden the remaining members financially.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Shion,,"The public beds are predictably cheap, but the real issue is the labor. Last year's cooking duty took two hours daily. If we don't find a place with catering, we're just trading training time for kitchen chores.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Minato,,I found out that public bookings are really scary! There's a lottery and a nine-page application that you have to redo if anything changes. It sounds like it would take a lot of time and effort to organize.,"{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"@Asuka, you're right. The transport costs are highly volatile, and those non-refundable deposits are a major risk. If we miscalculate the attendance, the club account or the members will have to cover the gap.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Takumi,,"Listen up! I found out that a fifth of the members didn't even show up to the away camps, and most of them quit the club shortly after. That's a disaster! We're losing people because we aren't bonding.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Takumi, while bonding is important, we cannot ignore the financial instability. If we choose a distant location with rigid booking terms, the risk of a deficit increases, which would only create more tension among the members.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Shion,,"@Takumi, your ""disaster"" is a symptom of poor planning. If people are quitting, it's likely because the camp experience was draining rather than bonding. We need to prioritize the quality of the stay, not just the ""vibe.""","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Minato,,"@Shion, I agree. If the people organizing it have to spend so much time on paperwork and cooking, they might not have any energy left to enjoy the camp with everyone else. That would be very sad.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Minato, that is a valid point. However, we must also consider the financial burden. If we choose a venue that is too expensive or has rigid terms, the stress of a budget deficit will be just as draining as the paperwork.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Asuka, @Shion, you're both missing the point! If people are quitting the club, the budget doesn't even matter because we won't have a club left! The seniors said mixing only happens when everyone sleeps in the same place. We need that!","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Asuka"",""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Takumi, sleeping in the same place does not justify a system where a few members pay for those who cancel. We must find a balance. A local venue would minimize transport volatility and financial risk while still allowing for shared space.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Shion,,"@Takumi, your obsession with ""sleeping in the same place"" is naive. If the environment is poor, shared space only amplifies the misery. We need a venue that ensures actual rest and minimal labor, or the ""bonding"" will just be shared exhaustion.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Minato,,"@Takumi, I understand you want everyone to be close, but I'm worried about the people who have to do all the work. If the booking is a lottery and there's so much paperwork, it might be too hard for them.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Takumi, I understand your desire for bonding, but we cannot ignore the financial reality. If we choose a high-risk booking and end up with a deficit, it will create resentment, which is the opposite of bonding. We need a stable plan.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Takumi,,"@Misaki, @Asuka, you're talking about ""resentment"" over money, but what about the resentment of the people who feel like outsiders in their own club? That's what's killing us! We need a place where we're all together, no matter what!","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Misaki"",""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"@Takumi, resentment over financial unfairness is just as damaging as social isolation. If we force a high-risk arrangement, we risk alienating members further. We must prioritize a destination that is both accessible and financially sustainable for everyone.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Shion,,"@Takumi, you're arguing from emotion, not logic. Forcing people into a shared space without ensuring quality rest and minimal labor is a recipe for failure. We need a professional facility, not a gamble on ""vibes"" that leaves us exhausted.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Minato,,"I think we should be very careful. If the organizers are too tired from cooking and paperwork, they can't help the others bond. Let's find a place that is kind to everyone's time and feelings.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Misaki,,"@Takumi, I understand your passion, but stability is the foundation of a good experience. If we face another budget shortfall, it will be a burden on the club's future. We need a plan that is financially responsible and low-risk.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Takumi,,"You're all just playing it safe while the club falls apart! If we only care about ""stability"" and ""low risk,"" we're just choosing to let the club die slowly. We need to be brave and pick a place that actually works!","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
