60,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"Looking at the options, Option B is the only responsible choice. It eliminates the volatility of transport costs and the risk of non-refundable deposits, ensuring that no member is unfairly burdened by late cancellations.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Shion,,"Option B is a compromise of convenience, but Option C is the only one that addresses the labor issue. Professional catering is a necessity; I refuse to waste training hours on kitchen chores again.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Minato,,"Option A sounds really scary because of that lottery and the nine-page application I found. I'm worried the organizers will be too tired to have fun. Option C has meals, which sounds very kind to the staff!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Misaki,,"@Shion, @Minato, while catering is convenient, Option C is a financial gamble. The distance will spike transport costs, and a whole-building let means non-refundable deposits. We cannot risk another budget deficit. Option B is the safest.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Shion"",""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Takumi,,"Option B is a joke! If we stay on campus, people will just go home or stick to their usual cliques. We'll be right back where we started. Option C is the only way to actually force us to bond!","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Takumi, forcing people to bond through a high-risk financial arrangement is counterproductive. If we choose Option C and face a deficit due to cancellations, the resulting resentment will destroy any sense of unity. Stability is the only way to ensure fairness.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Shion,,"@Asuka, stability is a baseline, not a goal. Option B is merely avoiding effort. If we want a camp that actually functions, we need professional services. Option C removes the labor burden, which is the only way to ensure we aren't exhausted.","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Minato,,"@Takumi, I really want us to bond too, but I'm worried about the people who have to organize it. If we pick Option A, the paperwork sounds like a nightmare. Option C seems much kinder to the organizers' time.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Minato, I understand your concern for the organizers, but we must be realistic. Option C's distance and rigid booking terms are a recipe for financial instability. We cannot prioritize convenience over the club's solvency. Option B is the only responsible choice.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Misaki, you're so obsessed with the money that you're ignoring the people! If we stay on campus, the people who already feel like outsiders just won't come. Option C gets us away from everything and puts us in one building. That's how you save a club!","{""words"":46,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Takumi, the ""outsiders"" you mention will be the first to suffer if the cost per person spikes because of a few cancellations. Option B allows us to control the budget and ensure that no one is financially penalized for others' absences.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Shion,,"@Takumi, your desperation for ""bonding"" is blinding you to the physical reality. Option A's shared dorms are a gamble on sleep quality, and Option B is a lack of ambition. Option C is the only logical choice for actual recovery.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Minato,,"@Asuka, @Misaki, I understand that money is important, but I'm really worried about the people who have to do the work. If we pick Option B, will they still have to do a lot of organizing? I just want everyone to be happy.","{""words"":43,""mentions"":[""Asuka"",""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Minato, Option B is the most considerate for the organizers because it minimizes the administrative burden and financial risk. We can't be ""happy"" if we're stressed about a budget shortfall. I vote for Option B.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Takumi,,"@Misaki, you're just choosing the easy way out! If we don't take a risk now, we're just waiting for the club to vanish. Option C is the only one that actually changes things. I vote for Option C!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Asuka,,"@Takumi, risk for the sake of risk is not leadership; it is negligence. Option C's financial structure is fundamentally unfair to the members. For the stability and fairness of the club, I vote for Option B.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Shion,,"@Takumi, your passion is irrelevant if the members are too exhausted to function. Option A is a gamble on sleep, and Option B is a lack of ambition. Option C ensures professional catering and a dedicated space. I vote for Option C.","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Minato,,"I'm really torn because I want everyone to bond, but I can't stop thinking about the organizers. Option A's paperwork is too scary, and Option B might be too boring. Option C is the kindest to the staff. I vote for Option C!","{""words"":43,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Misaki,,"@Minato, @Shion, I understand the appeal of catering and bonding, but we cannot ignore the financial risk. A deficit would be a burden on everyone. For the club's stability, I must prioritize the most responsible choice. I vote for Option B.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Minato"",""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Takumi,,"You're all just too scared to do what's necessary! If we pick Option B, we're just admitting we've given up on the club's spirit. I'm fighting for the people who are slipping away. I vote for Option C!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
